  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enabling Environment for self employment opportunities created</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The learning by doing approach will be used. Two areas of strategic emphasis will be especially important to ensuring that the resources invested lead to sustained results:
&#x2022;	Building systems of regular data collection on Decent Work and SDG employment indicators: The planned labour force survey and population census instruments will be designed not as isolated activities but rather as catalysts for establishing regular SDG employment data collection systems. 
&#x2022;	Building multiplier effects into training: Training efforts will also be designed not as one-time events but with lasting multiplier effects in mind. This will be accomplished in a number of ways: training participants will be individuals/institutions in a position to act as local resource persons/institutions, able to transmit their knowledge to others within their respective institutions; and a national ownership of the SDG employment indicators will be established. The mains outputs are:
-	National capacity built in decent work indicators in the context of SDG;
-	Labour force report;
-	 Improved labour market indicators through population census.</narrative>
  </description>
